        "paragraphs": [
          "Learned settings are the numbers training adjusts. Choose starting values for specific weights or bias arrays in the supplied model. A seed repeats the same random starting choices without changing the training random stream.",
          "Normal chooses values around a center with a chosen spread; Zeros makes selected values zero. Xavier and Kaiming choose a spread from incoming or outgoing connection counts. The typed owner selector uses actual model arrays, with no code or handwritten answers.",
          "Connect Starting settings and Supplied SGD to Train. Compare measured differences from an independent reference for starting arrays, predictions, the first adjustment, repeated draws and saved-weight reuse. Zero difference means match; these checks do not claim prediction quality or full training continuation."
